    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_49299b7d38e9ac1c0ff1a8a332863d3588e55e3394fdb3f294d67a33f75a5733",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Farey rank error is first rewritten in Bernoulli-Mobius coordinates, so its squared discrepancy becomes a sum of pairwise Bernoulli correlations. The generalized Dedekind three-term relation then permits cyclic symmetrization of the resulting triple sum, replacing the three correlation orientations by explicit gcd corrections that cancel down to Franel's exact quadratic identity.",
