    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8fc4eb32e5088425c77bf9d04a8b9b55f8388e6dc31618527e8f0e085bccf8f3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Lemma 3 first removes Farey coprimality by replacing it with Mobius-weighted unrestricted denominator sums. Bernoulli expansion then expresses centered power moments as finite combinations of the S_{r-1} family, while the Kubert distribution relation makes a full nonodd Kubert sum a nonzero scalar multiple of S_{s-1}; Lemma 2 turns square-root cancellation for each admissible S-index into the zero-free quotient condition zeta(z+s)/zeta(z) equivalent to RH.",
